# 24 - Delta Time Travel Practical (Databricks Must)

This practical covers:
- What is time travel
- VERSION AS OF
- TIMESTAMP AS OF
- Restore Delta table
- Real use cases (audit, debugging, rollback)

---

## 0) Setup

Use Databricks for best experience.

---

## 1) Create Delta Table

```python
data_v1 = [
    (1, "Pramod", 50000),
    (2, "Akash", 60000),
    (3, "Rahul", 45000)
]

df_v1 = spark.createDataFrame(data_v1, ["id", "name", "salary"])

delta_path = "/tmp/delta/employees_time_travel"

df_v1.write.format("delta").mode("overwrite").save(delta_path)
```

---

## 2) Update Delta Table (Create new version)

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import col

df_current = spark.read.format("delta").load(delta_path)

df_v2 = df_current.withColumn(
    "salary",
    col("salary") + 5000
)

df_v2.write.format("delta").mode("overwrite").save(delta_path)
```

Now Delta has multiple versions.

---

## 3) Check Delta History

```python
spark.sql(f"DESCRIBE HISTORY delta.`{delta_path}`").show(truncate=False)
```

You will see:
- version numbers
- operation type
- timestamp

---

## 4) Read Old Version (VERSION AS OF)

Example: read version 0

```python
df_old = spark.read.format("delta").option("versionAsOf", 0).load(delta_path)
df_old.show()
```

---

## 5) Read Using TIMESTAMP AS OF

First get timestamp from history, then:

```python
df_ts = spark.read.format("delta")     .option("timestampAsOf", "2026-02-07T00:00:00.000+0000")     .load(delta_path)

df_ts.show()
```

⚠️ timestamp should match your history timestamp.

---

## 6) SQL Time Travel

```python
spark.sql(f"SELECT * FROM delta.`{delta_path}` VERSION AS OF 0").show()
```

---

## 7) Restore Delta Table (Rollback)

Restore to version 0:

```python
spark.sql(f"RESTORE TABLE delta.`{delta_path}` TO VERSION AS OF 0")
```

Verify:

```python
spark.read.format("delta").load(delta_path).show()
```

---

## 8) Real Use Cases

✅ Audit: who changed what and when  
✅ Debugging: compare data between versions  
✅ Rollback: restore stable version  
✅ Data quality fixes  

---

## 9) Summary

- Delta stores versions automatically.
- You can read older versions using versionAsOf or timestampAsOf.
- RESTORE is used to rollback.

